  "response_text": "When we exit the SVC handler with the magic return code\u00a00xFFFFFFFD, the CPU expects the Process Stack Pointer (PSP) to already reference a correctly aligned, eight-word \u201cexception frame\u201d (xPSR, PC, LR, R12, R3\u2013R0) for the thread we\u2019re about to resume. If we skip\u00a0__set_PSP, that register still holds zero or stale data, so on the way out of Handler mode the core tries to pop those eight words from an invalid or mis-aligned address. The attempt triggers a MemManage or BusFault that escalates into a HardFault, and the program dies before the thread ever executes. Properly seeding PSP ensures the unstacking hardware reads valid memory and the thread starts cleanly.\\n",
